</note>
<note>
<title>Web Clip: Article on Async Patterns</title>
<content><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div><b>Understanding Async Patterns</b></div>
<div><br/></div>
<div>Clipped excerpt covering common async/await pitfalls and a comparison table of concurrency primitives.</div>
<div><br/></div>
<table style="border-collapse:collapse;">
<tr><th style="border:1px solid #999;padding:4px;">Primitive</th><th style="border:1px solid #999;padding:4px;">Use case</th></tr>
<tr><td style="border:1px solid #999;padding:4px;">Mutex</td><td style="border:1px solid #999;padding:4px;">Exclusive access to shared state</td></tr>
<tr><td style="border:1px solid #999;padding:4px;">Semaphore</td><td style="border:1px solid #999;padding:4px;">Limiting concurrent access</td></tr>
<tr><td style="border:1px solid #999;padding:4px;">Channel</td><td style="border:1px solid #999;padding:4px;">Message passing between tasks</td></tr>
</table></en-note>]]></content>
<created>20260415T193000Z</created>
<updated>20260415T193000Z</updated>
